<Item XName="FBMC_Source Measurement" UserName="FBMC_Source Measurement" Type="Notes">
<Selected><T>Bool</T><D>0</D></Selected>
<Text>&lt;FONT size=2&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/FONT&gt; &#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P style=&quot;BORDER-BOTTOM: windowtext 0.75pt solid; BORDER-LEFT: medium none; PADDING-BOTTOM: 1pt; MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; PADDING-LEFT: 0in; PADDING-RIGHT: 0in; BORDER-TOP: medium none; BORDER-RIGHT: medium none; PADDING-TOP: 0in&quot; class=MsoTitle align=center&gt;&lt;FONT size=5 face=Arial&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-FAMILY: Arial; FONT-SIZE: 18pt&quot;&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;FBMC_Source&amp;nbsp; Measurement&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot; class=MsoBodyText align=center&gt;&lt;FONT size=2&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-FAMILY: Arial; FONT-SIZE: 10pt; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt&quot;&gt;Keysight Technologies SystemVue Example Workspace&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;?xml:namespace prefix = o /&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P style=&quot;TEXT-ALIGN: center; MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot; class=MsoNormal align=center&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT face=&quot;Times New Roman&quot;&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT face=&quot;Times New Roman&quot;&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P style=&quot;TEXT-ALIGN: left; MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot; class=MsoNormal align=left&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt&quot;&gt;This&amp;nbsp;example workspace&amp;nbsp;demonstrates&amp;nbsp;spectrum performance for a FBMC&amp;nbsp;system in&amp;nbsp;AWGN (Additive White Gaussian Noise) channel&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT size=2&gt;. Performance of FBMC system is compared with that of OFDM system. Two implementations are given for FBMC system. The number of FFT points is extended to implement the filter bank and PPN_FFT is also provided to reduce computational complexity. OQAM&amp;nbsp;is adopted in the FBMC syetem. The frame of FBMC is composed of preamble symbols and data symbols. Preamble&amp;nbsp;is consist of two superimposed ZC (Zadoff-Chu) sequence. &lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P style=&quot;TEXT-ALIGN: left; MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot; class=MsoNormal align=left&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt&quot;&gt;Narrow band FBMC source and wideband FBMC source are provided in this example. &lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt&quot;&gt;A simple EVM model is provided to measure the EVM. SNR could be set in the Equations.&amp;nbsp;A&amp;nbsp;amplifier&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;is added to wideband FBMC source to simulate the&amp;nbsp;performance&amp;nbsp;result from wideband transmission system in mmwave.&amp;nbsp;This amplifier&amp;nbsp;could also be repalced with other RF transmit model designed by user.&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt&quot;&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P style=&quot;TEXT-ALIGN: left; MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot; class=MsoNormal align=left&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt&quot;&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;&lt;FONT size=3&gt;Simulation Instruction&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;OL type=1&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;LI style=&quot;LINE-HEIGHT: normal; MARGIN: 0in 0in 10pt; mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in&quot; class=MsoNormal&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;,&apos;serif&apos;; FONT-SIZE: 10pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;Set the &apos;NumSubcarriers&apos; parameter&amp;nbsp; to define the number of&amp;nbsp; total subcarriers.&lt;?xml:namespace prefix = o ns = &quot;urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:office&quot; /&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/LI&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;LI style=&quot;LINE-HEIGHT: normal; MARGIN: 0in 0in 10pt; mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in&quot; class=MsoNormal&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;,&apos;serif&apos;; FONT-SIZE: 10pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;The&amp;nbsp;&apos;ActiveSubcAlloc&apos; parameter&amp;nbsp;defined the&amp;nbsp;allocation of&amp;nbsp;active subcarriers. This parameter is a array and the fisrt row of the array is the beginning allocation of&amp;nbsp;active subcarriers and the second row is the end allocation of&amp;nbsp;active subcarriers.The range of the array is from&amp;nbsp;-NumSubc/2 to NumSubc/2-1. According to &quot;ActiveSubcAlloc&quot;, &amp;nbsp;the &apos;NumActiveSubc&apos; parameter acting as active subcarriers number is given in the equations.&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/LI&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;LI style=&quot;LINE-HEIGHT: normal; MARGIN: 0in 0in 10pt; mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in&quot; class=MsoNormal&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;,&apos;serif&apos;; FONT-SIZE: 10pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;The &apos;FilterOverlapFactor&apos; parameter is the overlapping factor of prototye filter used in FBMC system and three options of &apos;FilterOverlapFactor&apos; is provided in the example with corresponding frequency coefficients in frequency domain defined as parament &apos;FilterCoef&apos;. Parament &apos;FilterCoef&apos; is defined as a column vector and the elements in odd&amp;nbsp;row are negative and&amp;nbsp; the elements in&amp;nbsp;even&amp;nbsp;row are positive. The three cases of &apos;FilterOverlapFactor&apos; in 5G_FBMC_Source is 2,3 and 4. Correspondingly the parameter &#x2018;FilterCoef&#x2019; should be changed to [1,-sqrt(2)/2],[1,-0.911438,0.411438] and [1,-0.971960,sqrt(2)/2,-0.235147]. &lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;,&apos;serif&apos;; FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/LI&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;LI style=&quot;LINE-HEIGHT: normal; MARGIN: 0in 0in 10pt; mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in&quot; class=MsoNormal&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;,&apos;serif&apos;; FONT-SIZE: 10pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;The &apos;NumPreambleSyms&apos; and &apos;NumDataSyms&apos; define the number of preamble symbols and data symbols in one frame. In order to make repeat structure in preamble, &apos;NumPreambleSyms&apos; should be no less than &apos;FilterOverlapFactor&apos;+2.&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/LI&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;LI style=&quot;LINE-HEIGHT: normal; MARGIN: 0in 0in 10pt; mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in&quot; class=MsoNormal&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;,&apos;serif&apos;; FONT-SIZE: 10pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;In order to see attenuation of the spectrum, the&amp;nbsp;&apos;OversampleRatio&apos; parameter is used to define oversample&amp;nbsp;ratio. &lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/LI&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;LI style=&quot;LINE-HEIGHT: normal; MARGIN: 0in 0in 10pt; mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in&quot; class=MsoNormal&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;,&apos;serif&apos;; FONT-SIZE: 10pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;The &apos;FilterBankStructure&apos; is used to choose the implementation&amp;nbsp;of FBMC. Extended IFFT and PPN_IFFT is provided.&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/LI&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;LI style=&quot;LINE-HEIGHT: normal; MARGIN: 0in 0in 10pt; mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in&quot; class=MsoNormal&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;,&apos;serif&apos;; FONT-SIZE: 10pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;Pilots is also offered. The &apos;PilotsEnable&apos; is defined to use pilot or not. If pilot is uesd, the &apos;PilotIndex&apos; parameter defined the subcarriers that allocated to pilot and the &apos;PilotSequence&apos; is the value of pilot. The number of &apos;PilotIndex&apos; should be equal to the number of data in &apos;PilotSquence.&apos;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/LI&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;LI style=&quot;LINE-HEIGHT: normal; MARGIN: 0in 0in 10pt; mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in&quot; class=MsoNormal&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;,&apos;serif&apos;; FONT-SIZE: 10pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;Parameter &apos;PreambleEnable&apos; is provided in FBMC_Source to generate FBMC signal with/without preamble. Make sure &apos;PreambleEnable&apos; is set to &apos;YES&apos; when FBMC_Receiver is used. FBMC_Receiver is used in FBMC_EVM too.&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/LI&gt;&lt;/OL&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;</Text>
